OL,3,AManchester Arena survivor says 'I
OL,4,Athought life was over' on UK's first
OL,5,Anational day for terror victims
OL,6,
OL,7,FWhile taking place in London, the
OL,8,Fceremony will be broadcast live at a
OL,9,Fchurch in Lockerbie - the site of the
OL,10,Fdeadliest terror attack on UK soil,
OL,11,Fwrites our reporter in Scotland
OL,13,FA survivor of the 2017 Manchester Arena
OL,14,Fbombing tells the BBC "I thought life
OL,15,Fwas over for me", and says he felt
OL,16,F"forgotten about" when he left hospital
OL,18,FMeanwhile, Thelma Stober, who lost a
OL,19,Fleg in the London bombings of 7 July
OL,20,F2005, says today is "for people to
OL,21,Fremember that we are innocent victims
OL,22,Fof an attack"
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
